<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian April manufacturing input prices fall.</title>
<headline>Australian April manufacturing input prices fall.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian manufacturing input prices fell 0.5 percent in April from the previous month and were 3.8 percent lower than a year earlier, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Lower prices for crude oil were the main contributors to the decrease in the index,&quot; the bureau said.</p>
<p>This was partly offset by higher prices for a number of agricultural materials and imported chemicals.</p>
<p>The index for imported materials rose 0.1 percent in the month but fell 7.0 percent annually, while domestic materials fell 0.9 percent in April and 1.7 percent annually.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
